    "\"FINAL_ANSWER: {:result \\\"# Catering Plan: Ratatouille for 60\\\\n\\\\n## Scaled Ingredients\\\\n- 20 units Eggplant (large)\\\\n- 30 units Zucchini (medium)\\\\n- 30 units Yellow Squash (medium)\\\\n- 60 units Roma Tomatoes\\\\n- 20 units Red Bell Pepper\\\\n- 20 units Yellow Bell Pepper\\\\n- 10 units Yellow Onion (diced)\\\\n- 20 cloves Garlic (minced)\\\\n- 120 oz Crushed Tomatoes (canned)\\\\n- 40 fl oz Olive Oil\\\\n- 10 sprigs Fresh Thyme\\\\n- 7 tsp Salt\\\\n- 7 tsp Black Pepper\\\\n- 8 tsp Herbes de Provence\\\\n\\\\n## Revised Technique\\\\nTo maintain structural integrity for 60 servings, avoid a single deep pot which leads to bottom-layer crushing and steaming rather than sautéing. Utilize a two-stage batching strategy:\\\\n1. **High-Heat Sear:** Use multiple sheet pans or a large tilt skillet to roast/sear the eggplant, zucchini, and squash in batches. This evaporates excess moisture and develops color without the weight of the veg mashing itself.\\\\n2. **The Marriage:** Combine the seared vegetables with the tomato base in shallow hotel pans rather than a tall stockpot. This ensures even heat distribution and allows for gentle folding.\\\\n3. **Moisture Control:** Salt the eggplant 30 minutes prior to cooking to draw out water; pat dry before searing to prevent a \\\\\\\"spongy\\\\\\\" texture in the final mass.\\\\n\\\\n## Workflow & Station Setup\\\\n**Station A (Prep - 2 person team):**\\\\n- Focused on 1cm precision dicing. Use a \\\\\\\"mandoline-to-knife\\\\\\\" workflow for the squash and eggplant to ensure uniform cubes.\\\\n- Separate bins for high-moisture veg (zucchini/squash) and dense veg (peppers/onions).\\\\n- Tomato station: Concasse the Romas (blanch/shock/peel) to ensure skins don't toughen during service.\\\\n\\\\n**Station B (Cook - 1 person team):**\\\\n- Stage 1: Roast eggplant and squash on oiled parchment-lined sheet pans at 425°F (218°C) until golden (approx. 15-20 mins).\\\\n- Stage 2: Sauté onions, peppers, and garlic in the tilt skillet.\\\\n- Stage 3: Incorporate crushed tomatoes and herbs to create the \\\\\\\"sauce\\\\\\\" base.\\\\n- Stage 4: Combine all elements into 2-inch hotel pans for the final simmer.\\\\n\\\\n## Timing & Service\\\\n- **Prep (Dicing/Mise en place):** 2.5 hours (requires significant labor for 1cm dice across 200+ lbs of produce).\\\\n- **Initial Sear/Roast:** 45 minutes (staggered batches).\\\\n- **Aromatic Sweat (Onions/Peppers):** 20 minutes (longer time needed to soften 10 onions in bulk).\\\\n- **Combined Simmer:** 30–40 minutes. Note: Large thermal mass in hotel pans requires 15 minutes just to reach a simmer; do not rush this, or the flavors won't meld.\\\\n- **Resting:** 20 minutes (allows flavors to settle before service).\\\\n\\\\n## Cost Estimate\\\\nEggplant: $30.0\\\\n- Zucchini: $18.0\\\\n- Yellow Squash: $19.5\\\\n- Roma Tomatoes: $30.0\\\\n- Bell Peppers (Red/Yellow): $50.0\\\\n- Yellow Onion: $4.0\\\\n- Garlic: $2.0\\\\n- Crushed Tomatoes: $9.6\\\\n- Olive Oil: $10.0\\\\n- Salt and Spices: $3.5\\\\n- Fresh Herbs: $5.0\\\\n\\\\n**Total Estimated Supplier Cost: $181.6**\\\\n\\\\n## Pitfalls & Mitigations\\\\n- **Pitfall: The \\\\\\\"Mush\\\\\\\" Factor.** In deep vessels, the weight of 60 portions will pulverize the zucchini.\\\\n  *Mitigation:* Never stir aggressively. Use a folding motion with a large rubber spatula or flat paddle. Limit the depth of the product to 3 inches in any container.\\\\n- **Pitfall: Heat Distribution.** Large batches of tomato sauce can scorch on the bottom of a tilt skillet or pot.\\\\n  *Mitigation:* If using a tilt skillet, maintain a lower temperature once tomatoes are added and stir frequently. If using an oven-finish in hotel pans, cover with foil to retain moisture.\\\\n- **Pitfall: Service Holding.** Ratatouille continues to cook under heat lamps or in steam tables.\\\\n  *Mitigation:* Undercook the zucchini and squash slightly (al dente). The carry-over heat during the holding period will bring them to perfect tenderness by the time the 60th plate is served.\\\"}\"",
